  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch08-09> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch08-09--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch08-09--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch08-09: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.75" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.749"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The combinatorial component can be checked exactly and observations can test the empirical universality. Existing images cover important cases, but not every plant and animal drawing or all interpretations of the thirteen-type classification." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Enumerate admissible planar contact graphs for eight surface-reaching cells under triple-junction constraints, then classify observed eight-cell aggregates and test whether all fit exactly thirteen types." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The mathematical count depends sensitively on unstated equivalence and admissibility conventions.", "Observed 3D contacts can be ambiguous near vertices." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/thompson1917-ch08-09--gpt--dataset-1> .
